 **Day 31 of My AI Builder Series: Build an AI Supply Chain Control Tower**

Today's project explores one of the most impactful capabilities in modern operations—an **AI-powered Supply Chain Control Tower**.

In today's dynamic business environment, supply chains don't fail because of a single disruption—they fail when organizations lack real-time visibility and the ability to respond quickly. A Supply Chain Control Tower provides a centralized view of logistics, inventory, supplier performance, and transportation, enabling operations leaders to make informed decisions before minor issues escalate into major business challenges.

Using **Claude**, I built an interactive simulation that replicates how enterprise operations teams monitor live disruptions, prioritize critical alerts, and make strategic decisions based on changing business conditions.

### What I Built

✅ **Real-Time Control Tower**
Monitor inventory levels, supplier performance, transportation status, and logistics disruptions through a centralized operational dashboard.

✅ **Operational Decision Engine**
Evaluate competing priorities and make decisions that balance service levels, operational costs, inventory optimization, business continuity, and customer commitments.

✅ **Business KPI Impact**
Visualize how every operational decision influences key enterprise metrics, including customer satisfaction, inventory availability, transportation costs, supplier performance, sustainability, and revenue.

✅ **Interactive Enterprise Dashboard**
Developed using **HTML, CSS, and JavaScript**, delivering a premium, enterprise-grade dashboard experience that mirrors real-world supply chain control towers.

### Key Learning

This simulation provides participants with a practical understanding of how interconnected decisions shape supply chain performance. By systematically applying and evaluating multiple strategic levers, users experience how balanced decision-making can optimize cost, mitigate risk, improve sustainability, and enhance customer outcomes. The integration of AI-powered guidance further enriches the experience by delivering data-driven insights that support more informed and effective operational decisions.

The biggest value of AI isn't replacing operations leaders—it's empowering them with greater visibility, faster analysis, and better decision support. Interactive simulations like this help transform supply chain learning from static theory into immersive, hands-on experiences where every decision has measurable business impact.

